WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.099 --> 00:00:15.800
over to Grace.

2
00:00:19.781 --> 00:00:21.761
think something happened to your neighbor!"

3
00:00:21.781 --> 00:00:24.642
"Why do you think that?"

4
00:00:25.102 --> 00:00:25.882
Grace asked.

5
00:00:27.123 --> 00:00:28.923
Daisy traded a look with Kaleem.

6
00:00:28.943 --> 00:00:34.893
"Well, um, her dog sounds upset," Kaleem said.

7
00:00:34.913 --> 00:00:36.773
"Maybe we should check on her."

8
00:00:36.793 --> 00:00:41.755
"Scamp does seem anxious today," Grace said.

9
00:00:41.775 --> 00:00:44.075
"He's usually really happy.

10
00:00:44.095 --> 00:00:47.736
I guess it wouldn't hurt to check on Mrs.

11
00:00:47.816 --> 00:00:49.176
Ortiz, just in case.

12
00:00:49.897 --> 00:00:51.417
She's a very nice neighbor."

13
00:00:57.659 --> 00:01:00.620
They went back through Grace's house and over to Mrs.

14
00:01:00.680 --> 00:01:02.000
Ortiz's front door.

15
00:01:04.652 --> 00:01:06.654
Daisy knocked, but nobody answered.

16
00:01:06.674 --> 00:01:09.215
"Let's try again," Kaleem said.

17
00:01:09.235 --> 00:01:14.999
"Louder!" Daisy knocked as hard as she could, but there was still no response.

18
00:01:15.019 --> 00:01:18.522
"I guess she's not home," Grace said with a shrug.

19
00:01:19.643 --> 00:01:23.285
The friendly chickadee flew over just in time to hear Grace.

20
00:01:23.305 --> 00:01:26.688
"Is she talking about the old lady who lives here?"

21
00:01:27.008 --> 00:01:27.868
the bird asked.

22
00:01:27.888 --> 00:01:30.130
"I just looked in through the window.

23
00:01:30.810 --> 00:01:32.672
She's lying very still on the floor."

24
00:01:33.632 --> 00:01:35.333
Daisy gasped.

25
00:01:36.154 --> 00:01:36.854
"Oh, no!"

26
00:01:37.635 --> 00:01:39.096
Grace looked surprised.

27
00:01:39.116 --> 00:01:40.517
"What's wrong?"

28
00:01:40.537 --> 00:01:43.419
"Which window?"

29
00:01:43.739 --> 00:01:44.960
Daisy asked the bird.

30
00:01:45.640 --> 00:01:47.301
Now Grace looked confused.

31
00:01:48.442 --> 00:01:50.263
But Daisy wasn't paying attention.

32
00:01:51.444 --> 00:01:54.726
The chickadee flew over and pecked on a window nearby.

33
00:01:55.707 --> 00:01:57.548
Daisy ran over and looked through it.

34
00:02:00.308 --> 00:02:03.510
An older woman was lying on the floor, not moving.

35
00:02:03.530 --> 00:02:05.552
"Is that Mrs.

36
00:02:05.632 --> 00:02:07.373
Ortiz?" Daisy cried.

37
00:02:08.374 --> 00:02:09.895
Grace and Kaleem ran over.

38
00:02:09.915 --> 00:02:16.519
"We shouldn't be looking through people's windows," Grace said, hanging back.

39
00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:18.661
Kaleem stepped to the window.

40
00:02:18.681 --> 00:02:21.083
"Oh, no!"

41
00:02:21.543 --> 00:02:22.103
he cried.

42
00:02:22.123 --> 00:02:25.045
"Maybe she fainted or fell or something."

43
00:02:26.707 --> 00:02:28.408
Grace finally looked in too.

44
00:02:30.276 --> 00:02:31.357
"Mrs. Ortiz!

45
00:02:32.018 --> 00:02:34.079
Let's tell my parents to call for help."

46
00:02:37.082 --> 00:02:38.743
They ran back to Grace's house.

47
00:02:42.106 --> 00:02:43.507
Her parents were in the living room.

48
00:02:44.888 --> 00:02:48.211
A huge tropical fish tank took up most of one wall.

49
00:02:51.333 --> 00:02:52.694
Daisy took a deep breath.

50
00:02:52.714 --> 00:02:59.220
"Mrs. Ortiz's dog was barking a lot, so we went to check on her."

51
00:02:59.860 --> 00:03:01.401
"Yeah," Kaleem said.

52
00:03:01.421 --> 00:03:05.963
"We thought he, um, might be trying to tell us something."

53
00:03:07.404 --> 00:03:08.625
Grace's mom chuckled.

54
00:03:08.645 --> 00:03:14.028
"I'm sure Scamp is just barking because he's happy.

55
00:03:14.048 --> 00:03:17.029
He loves playing in the pool Mrs.

56
00:03:17.109 --> 00:03:18.270
Ortiz got for him."

57
00:03:18.290 --> 00:03:23.833
"But we saw her," Grace said.

58
00:03:23.853 --> 00:03:25.814
"Through the window.

59
00:03:26.554 --> 00:03:29.136
She's lying on the floor and not moving."

60
00:03:30.728 --> 00:03:32.309
"You peeked in her window?"

61
00:03:32.730 --> 00:03:34.971
Grace's dad sounded disapproving.

62
00:03:35.932 --> 00:03:37.773
But Grace's mom looked alarmed.

63
00:03:37.793 --> 00:03:39.774
"Which window?"

64
00:03:44.618 --> 00:03:46.139
The two adults rushed out.

65
00:03:48.200 --> 00:03:50.121
Daisy, Kaleem, and Grace followed.

66
00:03:56.746 --> 00:03:58.147
Scamp was still barking.

67
00:04:00.892 --> 00:04:01.772
"What's happening?

68
00:04:02.393 --> 00:04:03.833
Is my lady all right?"

69
00:04:03.853 --> 00:04:07.234
"It's okay, Scamp," Daisy called back.

70
00:04:07.254 --> 00:04:08.894
"We're checking on her."

71
00:04:10.035 --> 00:04:12.155
Grace gave Daisy another odd look.

72
00:04:12.815 --> 00:04:14.116
But she didn't say anything.

73
00:04:15.056 --> 00:04:17.917
Meanwhile Grace's dad was knocking on the door.

74
00:04:17.937 --> 00:04:19.297
"Mrs. Ortiz?"

75
00:04:19.677 --> 00:04:20.197
he called.

76
00:04:20.217 --> 00:04:21.678
"Are you all right?"

77
00:04:24.418 --> 00:04:26.499
Grace's mom peered in through the window.

78
00:04:26.519 --> 00:04:27.919
"Oh, no!

79
00:04:28.539 --> 00:04:30.160
We need to call for an ambulance!"

80
00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:40.122
While the adults made the call, Daisy hurried to tell Scamp what was happening.

81
00:04:40.142 --> 00:04:44.983
"Thank you," Scamp barked.

82
00:04:45.883 --> 00:04:47.644
A moment later his ears pricked up.

83
00:04:48.764 --> 00:04:50.064
"I hear a siren."

84
00:04:50.564 --> 00:04:51.925
Daisy couldn't hear anything.

85
00:04:52.625 --> 00:04:56.466
But she knew that dogs' hearing was much better than humans' hearing.

86
00:04:56.486 --> 00:04:58.727
"Phew!" she said.

87
00:04:58.747 --> 00:05:00.707
"Help is on the way!"
